#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128770 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "d180f745-028b-5859-8cad-4a49b5c20773" :question/math-academy-id "e-10521" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15} \\sum_{j=1}^{18} (a_{i} - 2)(b_{j}+1)$\n\ngiven that\n\n$\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15}a_i = 40, \\qquad \\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^{18}b_j =-8$." :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n a_{i}b_j = \\sum_{i=1}^m a_i \\sum_{j=1}^n b_{j}\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(15)∑_(j = 1)^(18)(a_{i} - 2)(b_{j} + 1) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(15)(a_{i} - 2)∑_(j = 1)^(18)(b_{j} + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(15)(a_{i} - 2)∑_(j = 1)^(18)(b_{j} + 1) &= (∑_(i = 1)^(15)a_{i} - ∑_(i = 1)^(15)2) \\cdot (∑_(j = 1)^(18)b_{j} + ∑_(j = 1)^(18)1) \\\\\n&= (∑_(i = 1)^(15)a_{i} - 2∑_(i = 1)^(15)1) \\cdot (∑_(j = 1)^(18)b_{j} + ∑_(j = 1)^(18)1) \\\\\n&= (40 - 2 \\cdot 15) \\cdot (-8 + 18) \\\\\n&= (10) \\cdot (10) \\\\\n&= 100\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128927 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8537cc22-8d18-57c8-9ebf-921bd4d06ae7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Summation"}] :question/id #uuid "e17f982d-3d3e-5279-b507-d390e4f1970f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6116" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^3\\sum_{i=1}^2 (i+j)$." :question/worked-solution "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(j = 1)^(3)∑_(i = 1)^(2)(i + j) &= ∑_(j = 1)^(3)[∑_(i = 1)^(2)(i + j)] \\\\\n&= ∑_(j = 1)^(3)[(1 + j) + (2 + j)] \\\\\n&= ∑_(j = 1)^(3)(3 + 2j)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the sum above by summing over the index $j$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(j = 1)^(3)(3 + 2j) &= (3 + 2 \\cdot 1) + (3 + 2 \\cdot 2) + (3 + 2 \\cdot 3) \\\\\n&= 5 + 7 + 9 \\\\\n&= 21\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128928 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "e8f3608f-68f2-5ba9-b618-447887e7f6fb" :question/math-academy-id "e-6118" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij})$\n\ngiven that\n\n$\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} a_{ij} = 8, \\qquad\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} b_{ij} = 15$." :question/worked-solution "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)(a_{ij} + b_{ij}) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)a_{ij} + ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)b_{ij}, \\\\\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)ka_{ij} &= k∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)a_{ij}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)(1 + 2a_{ij} - b_{ij}) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1 + ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)2a_{ij} - ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)b_{ij} \\\\\n&= (∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1) + 2∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)a_{ij} - ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)b_{ij} \\\\\n&= (∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1) + 2(8) - 15 \\\\\n&= (∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1) + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n 1 = mn\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1) + 1 &= 5 \\cdot 8 + 1 \\\\\n&= 40 + 1 \\\\\n&= 41\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij}) = 41\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "827c8e46-d0b0-5069-a187-6b461a964fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126417} {:answer/id #uuid "aceb1436-c191-5f85-87dc-5c27fd1e9567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126418} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b71b13-f56c-53ee-bd4e-1a63bfe35864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126419} {:answer/id #uuid "13743981-4143-5f77-b7c3-38e2482754ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126420} {:answer/id #uuid "484b317d-f202-5143-9eef-bee417679752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "484b317d-f202-5143-9eef-bee417679752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126421} :answer-field/id #uuid "def6dcec-0597-5a0d-82df-6c07ef5cf083" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126416}] :question/id #uuid "179c3108-3135-5849-a6a9-1775dfb4870a" :question/math-academy-id "q-149603" :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nFind the value of the double sum\n\n$∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(10)(1 - a_{ij} - b_{ij})$\n\ngiven that\n\n$∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(10)a_{ij} = 10, ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(10)b_{ij} = 20$." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8537cc22-8d18-57c8-9ebf-921bd4d06ae7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Summation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f0586c1-f847-5f1d-813e-201ffbe3602d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128517} {:a